{"name":"World’s Away","hex":"#03667b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"world","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The subjective human experience, regarded collectively; human collective existence; existence in general; the reality we live in.","The subjective human experience, regarded individually."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider or cause to be considered from a global perspective; to consider as a global whole, rather than making or focusing on national or other distinctions; compare globalize.","To make real; to make worldly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world"},{"term":"away","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["From a place, hence.","Aside; off; in another direction."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Away with you! Go away! Begone!"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away"}],"entries":[{"title":"World","blocks":[{"text":"A world is a totality of entities. In philosophy, the world is customarily viewed as all of existence or the whole of reality. Some conceptions see the world as unique, while others examine the character of entities that exist in the world or talk of a plurality of worlds, challenging the idea that the world is an all-inclusive whole. The term is also commonly used as a context-dependent expression to denote a specific domain of discourse and everything within it, such as the Earth and all life on it or the whole of human existence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Hubble_ultra_deep_field.jpg/330px-Hubble_ultra_deep_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Yggdrasil.jpg/500px-Yggdrasil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Yggdrasil.jpg/500px-Yggdrasil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yggdrasil, an attempt to reconstruct the Norse world tree which connects the heavens, the world, and the underworld.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYggdrasil.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png/500px-Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png/1280px-Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png/500px-Home_in_Relation_to_Everything.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scientific worldview","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHome_in_Relation_to_Everything.png"}],"sounds":{"world":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fb/En-us-world.oga?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fb/En-us-world.oga/En-us-world.oga.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/94/En-ca-world.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/94/En-ca-world.ogg/En-ca-world.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/ba/She_says_the_Third_Pole_is_one_of_the_world%E2%80%99s_largest_sources_of_fresh_drinking_water.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com